## 3. Elasticsearch documents

```java
@Document(indexName = "person-snapshots")
public class SnapshotDoc {
    @Id private String id;                     // clientId:personId
    @Field(type = FieldType.Keyword) private String clientId;
    @Field(type = FieldType.Keyword) private String personId;

    @Field(type = FieldType.Object, enabled = false)   // stored, not indexed → cheap
    private Map<String, Object> snapshot;             // what the client froze
    @Field(type = FieldType.Object, enabled = false)
    private Map<String, Object> lastNotifiedState;    // rolling baseline (design B)

    @Field(type = FieldType.Keyword) private String lastNotifiedHash;
    @Field(type = FieldType.Long)    private long   lastNotifiedVersion; // event version/offset
    @Field(type = FieldType.Date)    private Instant snapshotAt;

    @Version private Long version;             // maps to seq_no/primary_term → optimistic locking
    // getters/setters
}
```

Index settings: `enabled: false` on the blobs keeps indexing cost near zero; you only need `clientId` / `personId` searchable. Use 1 replica, `refresh_interval: 5s` (you never search-then-read the same doc in the hot path — you `GET` by id, which is real-time).

## 4. Kafka consumer pipeline

```java
@Component
@RequiredArgsConstructor
public class PersonChangeConsumer {

    private final KafkaReceiver<String, byte[]> receiver;   // built from ReceiverOptions
    private final ChangeProcessor processor;
    private final DeadLetterPublisher dlt;
    private final MeterRegistry metrics;

    @EventListener(ApplicationReadyEvent.class)
    public void start() {
        receiver.receive()
            // ordering per partition, parallelism across partitions
            .groupBy(rec -> rec.receiverOffset().topicPartition())
            .flatMap(partition -> partition
                    .concatMap(this::handle)          // strictly sequential inside a partition
                    .onErrorContinue((e, o) -> metrics.counter("consumer.unexpected").increment()),
                Integer.MAX_VALUE)                    // one lane per assigned partition
            .retryWhen(Retry.backoff(Long.MAX_VALUE, Duration.ofSeconds(1)).maxBackoff(Duration.ofSeconds(30)))
            .subscribe();
    }

    private Mono<Void> handle(ReceiverRecord<String, byte[]> rec) {
        return processor.process(rec.key(), rec.value(), rec.offset())
            .timeout(Duration.ofSeconds(30))
            .onErrorResume(e -> dlt.publish(rec, e))          // poison → DLT, don't block partition
            .doFinally(s -> rec.receiverOffset().acknowledge()); // at-least-once
    }
}
```

`ReceiverOptions` essentials:

```java
@Bean
KafkaReceiver<String, byte[]> receiver(KafkaProperties props) {
    Map<String, Object> cfg = new HashMap<>(props.buildConsumerProperties());
    cfg.put(ConsumerConfig.ENABLE_AUTO_COMMIT_CONFIG, false);
    cfg.put(ConsumerConfig.MAX_POLL_RECORDS_CONFIG, 500);
    cfg.put(ConsumerConfig.AUTO_OFFSET_RESET_CONFIG, "earliest");
    ReceiverOptions<String, byte[]> opts = ReceiverOptions.<String, byte[]>create(cfg)
        .subscription(List.of("people.updated", "people.deleted"))
        .commitInterval(Duration.ofSeconds(1))
        .commitBatchSize(200)
        .maxDeferredCommits(2_000);          // bounds in-flight uncommitted records
    return KafkaReceiver.create(opts);
}
```

## 5. Change processor (the core)

```java
@Service
@RequiredArgsConstructor
public class ChangeProcessor {

    private final ObjectMapper om;
    private final PersonStateStore personState;     // Redis: hash + version per person
    private final SubscriberIndex subscribers;      // Redis set: personId -> clientIds
    private final SnapshotRepository snapshots;     // ES reactive
    private final Notifier notifier;
    private final MeterRegistry metrics;

    private static final Set<String> VOLATILE = Set.of("updatedAt", "etag", "_ingestTs");

    public Mono<Void> process(String personId, byte[] payload, long offset) {
        JsonNode current = normalize(om.readTree(payload));   // strip volatile, sort keys
        String hash = Hashing.sha256().hashBytes(current.toString().getBytes(UTF_8)).toString();

        return personState.lastHash(personId)
            .defaultIfEmpty("")
            .flatMap(prev -> {
                if (prev.equals(hash)) {                       // fast path: no real change
                    metrics.counter("events.noop").increment();
                    return Mono.empty();
                }
                return fanOut(personId, current, hash, offset)
                    .then(personState.put(personId, hash, offset));
            });
    }

    private Mono<Void> fanOut(String personId, JsonNode current, String hash, long version) {
        return subscribers.clientsFor(personId)                // Flux<String>
            .collectList()
            .filter(l -> !l.isEmpty())
            .flatMapMany(clientIds ->
                snapshots.mget(clientIds.stream().map(c -> c + ":" + personId).toList()))
            .filter(doc -> !hash.equals(doc.getLastNotifiedHash()))       // idempotent on redelivery
            .filter(doc -> version > doc.getLastNotifiedVersion())        // ignore stale events
            .flatMap(doc -> notifyAndAdvance(doc, current, hash, version), 32) // bounded fan-out
            .then();
    }

    private Mono<Void> notifyAndAdvance(SnapshotDoc doc, JsonNode current, String hash, long version) {
        JsonNode baseline = om.valueToTree(doc.getLastNotifiedState() != null
                                           ? doc.getLastNotifiedState() : doc.getSnapshot());
        JsonNode patch = JsonDiff.asJson(baseline, current);   // RFC-6902 ops
        if (patch.isEmpty()) return Mono.empty();

        ChangeNotification n = new ChangeNotification(
            doc.getClientId(), doc.getPersonId(), version,
            doc.getClientId() + ":" + doc.getPersonId() + ":" + version,  // idempotency key
            patch);

        return notifier.send(n)
            .then(Mono.defer(() -> {
                doc.setLastNotifiedState(om.convertValue(current, Map.class));
                doc.setLastNotifiedHash(hash);
                doc.setLastNotifiedVersion(version);
                return snapshots.save(doc);                       // @Version → 409 on conflict
            }))
            .onErrorResume(OptimisticLockingFailureException.class, e -> Mono.empty()) // someone else advanced it
            .then();
    }

    private JsonNode normalize(JsonNode n) {
        ObjectNode o = ((ObjectNode) n).deepCopy();
        VOLATILE.forEach(o::remove);
        return om.readerFor(JsonNode.class)                       // ORDER_MAP_ENTRIES_BY_KEYS on the mapper
                 .readValue(o.toString());
    }
}
```

Note `version` here: prefer a **business version** from the event (e.g. `person.version`/`updatedAt` epoch). Fall back to Kafka offset only if all events for a person live on one partition of one topic.

## 6. Subscriber reverse index & person state (Redis)

```java
@Component @RequiredArgsConstructor
public class SubscriberIndex {
    private final ReactiveStringRedisTemplate redis;

    public Flux<String> clientsFor(String personId) {
        return redis.opsForSet().members("subs:" + personId);
    }
    // called by the bookmark API
    public Mono<Void> add(String clientId, String personId)    { return redis.opsForSet().add("subs:" + personId, clientId).then(); }
    public Mono<Void> remove(String clientId, String personId) { return redis.opsForSet().remove("subs:" + personId, clientId).then(); }
}

@Component @RequiredArgsConstructor
public class PersonStateStore {
    private final ReactiveStringRedisTemplate redis;
    public Mono<String> lastHash(String personId) { return redis.opsForHash().<String,String>get("pstate:" + personId, "h"); }
    public Mono<Void> put(String personId, String hash, long v) {
        return redis.opsForHash().putAll("pstate:" + personId, Map.of("h", hash, "v", Long.toString(v))).then();
    }
}
```

If you'd rather avoid Redis: `SubscriberIndex` can be an ES `terms` query on `person-snapshots` (`personId = X`, `_source: [clientId]`) — the snapshot index *is* the bookmark index then. Redis is ~10× cheaper per event though; use ES as a rebuild source for the Redis sets.

## 7. Snapshot creation API (bookmark)

```java
@RestController @RequestMapping("/clients/{clientId}/bookmarks") @RequiredArgsConstructor
public class BookmarkController {
    private final PersonReadService people;      // your source of current person state
    private final SnapshotRepository snapshots;
    private final SubscriberIndex subscribers;

    @PostMapping("/{personId}")
    public Mono<SnapshotDoc> bookmark(@PathVariable String clientId, @PathVariable String personId) {
        return people.current(personId)
            .map(state -> {
                SnapshotDoc d = new SnapshotDoc();
                d.setId(clientId + ":" + personId);
                d.setClientId(clientId); d.setPersonId(personId);
                d.setSnapshot(state); d.setLastNotifiedState(state);
                d.setLastNotifiedHash(hashOf(state)); d.setSnapshotAt(Instant.now());
                return d;
            })
            .flatMap(snapshots::save)
            .flatMap(d -> subscribers.add(clientId, personId).thenReturn(d));  // order: ES first, then Redis
    }

    @DeleteMapping("/{personId}")
    public Mono<Void> remove(@PathVariable String clientId, @PathVariable String personId) {
        return subscribers.remove(clientId, personId)
            .then(snapshots.deleteById(clientId + ":" + personId));
    }
}
```

`people.current(...)` — the best source is a **compacted Kafka topic** of person state materialized into Redis/ES (`person-current` index) by the same consumer, so the snapshot reflects exactly what the change detector sees.

## 8. Resilient notifier

```java
@Component @RequiredArgsConstructor
public class Notifier {
    private final WebClient client;   // baseUrl of notification service, pooled ConnectionProvider
    private final CircuitBreaker cb;  // resilience4j
    private final Retry retry;
    private final Bulkhead bulkhead;

    public Mono<Void> send(ChangeNotification n) {
        return client.post().uri("/notifications")
            .header("Idempotency-Key", n.idempotencyKey())
            .bodyValue(n)
            .retrieve()
            .onStatus(HttpStatusCode::is4xxClientError, r -> Mono.error(new NonRetryableException()))
            .toBodilessEntity()
            .timeout(Duration.ofSeconds(3))
            .transformDeferred(BulkheadOperator.of(bulkhead))
            .transformDeferred(RetryOperator.of(retry))            // exp backoff, ignore NonRetryable
            .transformDeferred(CircuitBreakerOperator.of(cb))
            .then();
    }
}
```

```yaml
resilience4j:
  retry.instances.notifier:
    max-attempts: 4
    wait-duration: 200ms
    enable-exponential-backoff: true
    ignore-exceptions: [com.acme.NonRetryableException]
  circuitbreaker.instances.notifier:
    sliding-window-size: 50
    failure-rate-threshold: 50
    wait-duration-in-open-state: 20s
  bulkhead.instances.notifier:
    max-concurrent-calls: 64
```

When the circuit is open, `notifyAndAdvance` errors → the record goes to the DLT (or better: to a `notifications.retry` topic with a delayed re-consumer), and the snapshot is **not** advanced, so nothing is lost.

## 9. Dead-letter / retry

```java
@Component @RequiredArgsConstructor
public class DeadLetterPublisher {
    private final KafkaSender<String, byte[]> sender;
    public Mono<Void> publish(ReceiverRecord<String, byte[]> rec, Throwable e) {
        ProducerRecord<String, byte[]> out = new ProducerRecord<>(rec.topic() + ".DLT", rec.key(), rec.value());
        out.headers().add("x-error", e.getClass().getName().getBytes(UTF_8))
                     .add("x-origin-offset", Long.toString(rec.offset()).getBytes(UTF_8));
        return sender.send(Mono.just(SenderRecord.create(out, null))).then();
    }
}
```

## 10. Operational checklist

- **Partitions**: set the people topic to ≥ the max consumer instances × 2; parallelism = partitions.
- **Rebalances**: use `CooperativeStickyAssignor` and keep `maxDeferredCommits` bounded so a rebalance doesn't replay thousands of records.
- **Idempotency is layered**: content hash (skip no-ops) → `lastNotifiedHash` per client (skip redeliveries) → `Idempotency-Key` header (notification service dedupes as last line of defense).
- **Deletes**: handle `people.deleted` (tombstone) by sending a "person removed" notification and marking the snapshot `tombstoned=true`; don't drop the doc so the client still sees their snapshot.
- **Hot persons** (one person bookmarked by 100k clients): the `mget` should be paginated — use `search_after` on `personId` with page size 1k and stream pages into the `flatMap`; the 32-wide fan-out limit keeps the notification service safe.
- **Rebuilding Redis**: a nightly job (or on cold start with empty Redis) scans `person-snapshots` with `_source: [clientId, personId]` and repopulates `subs:*`.
- **Metrics to alert on**: consumer lag per partition, `events.noop` ratio, notifier CB state, DLT rate, ES `version_conflict` rate, p99 end-to-end latency (Kafka timestamp → notification ack).
- **Testing**: Testcontainers (Kafka + ES + Redis) with a test that publishes N events for one person and asserts exactly one notification per real change, even under duplicate delivery.

If you tell me the shape of the person events (single topic vs. several partial-update topics, whether they carry a version field) and roughly how many bookmarks per person you expect, I can tune the fan-out and diff strategy further — e.g. several partial topics would push me toward a Kafka Streams / KTable join to assemble full state before diffing.
